### Conclusion on Metrics

The significance lies in knowing which metric solves your specific problem. Torque is about force; horsepower is about energy over time. For a user deciding how to drive, understanding that shifting late maximizes power delivery helps explain why sporty cars sound different and feel faster than economy vehicles designed for low-RPM torque efficiency.
